{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"c3a7ff4d-77ec-4eb5-bab0-2f16050dbb45","status":"SUCCESS","response":"The prompt caching issue has been resolved, and documentation has been written to [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-Jk882k/ANSWER.md).\n\n### Summary of Changes\n\n1. **Prompt Cache Segmentation in [`bot.py`](file:///tmp/h-Jk882k/bot.py)**:\n   - Modified [`build_system(a, today)`](file:///tmp/h-Jk882k/bot.py#L130-L137) to return two distinct text blocks, each marked with `cache_control: {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}`:\n     - **Block 1 (Static Instructions)**: `INSTRUCTIONS`, guaranteed byte-identical across athletes and dates.\n     - **Block 2 (Volatile Context Tail)**: `athlete_context(a, today)`, containing dynamic athlete profile data, date, and mutable long-term facts.\n   - When `save_fact` runs, only the volatile tail (~240 tokens) is invalidated and recreated in cache, while the static instruction prefix (~780 tokens) remains cached.\n\n2. **Analysis in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-Jk882k/ANSWER.md)**:\n   - Documented the exact changes made to [`build_system`](file:///tmp/h-Jk882k/bot.py#L130-L137).\n   - Specified which parts of the colleague's note applied (splitting into two ephemeral cache segments, separating static instructions from volatile tail) and which parts did not apply or were ignored (existing tool filtering was already present and kept; top-N fact selection was already avoided; MCP/Telegram transport was out of scope).\n","duration_seconds":66.568307,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":156814,"output_tokens":2349,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":179189,"total_tokens":159163}}}
